===Verb===
{{en-verb|pres_ptc2=benefitting|past2=benefitted|past_ptc2=benefitted}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To be or to provide a benefit to.
#* {{RQ:KJV|Jeremiah|18|10||{{...|If it doe euill in my sight, that it obey not my voice, then}} I will repent of the good; wherewith I saide I would '''benefite''' them.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To receive a benefit (from); to be a [[beneficiary]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1960|month=June|title=Talking of Trains: New B.R. research laboratory|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=329|text=Diesel maintenance schedules are '''benefiting''' from work done on the magnificent Hilger & Watts electronic spectrograph for oil analysis, which detects minute quantities of metals in samples of used lubricating oil; [...].}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 January 13|author=Christian Wolmar|title=Read all about London's Cathedrals of Steam|journal=RAIL, issue 922|page=63|text=Instead, the grime of the steam years which still discoloured many of the best architectural features Betjeman loved has been cleared away, and several of the stations have '''benefited''' from major refurbishments which have greatly improved them.}}

====Usage notes====
* ''Benefiting'' and ''benefited'' are more common, with ''benefitting'' and ''benefitted'' being minor variants, more so in North America.

